    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_73e80311",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: what_men_want; hasOverallIntent: Mysogynous; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a woman dressed as a football referee in a revealing outfit, holding a beer and a football, with the text 'what men want' overlaid. This visual juxtaposition maps onto the stereotype that men desire women who are hypersexualized and objectified, particularly in contexts like sports. The intent is to reinforce a misogynous trope by portraying the woman as a sexualized object whose value is tied to her appearance and availability, rather than her competence or agency. This aligns with the 'Mysogynous' toxicity category as it contains hate against women by reducing them to sexualized stereotypes and implying their worth is tied to their physical appearance and availability for male gratification.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_22a82220"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
